          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વર્તવું (vartvũ) goes back to Sanskrit vártatē, \"turns, moves; takes place\" (CDIAL 11352). CDIAL lists no Gujarati form; \"to behave\", to carry oneself, is the sense Gujarati gives it."
            }
          ]
